4 Commands
**********

4.1 sky init
============

Initialize QuickSky repository in current directory.

Prompts for:
* Username (for commit attribution)
* Remote repository URL
* Main branch name

4.2 sky upload [MESSAGE]
========================

Commit and push changes to remote repository.

If no message provided, auto-generates timestamped commit message.

Examples:
     sky upload "Fix login bug"
     sky upload

4.3 sky log
===========

View all commit records in reverse chronological order.

Shows SHA, author, timestamp, message, and file changes.

4.4 sky branch [OPTIONS] [NAME]
===============================

Branch management operations:

'-a NAME'
     Create and switch to new branch

'-d NAME'
     Delete branch (cannot delete current branch)

'NAME'
     Switch to existing branch

'(no args)'
     List all branches and show current branch

Examples:
     sky branch -a feature/payment
     sky branch main
     sky branch -d old-feature
     sky branch

4.5 sky change-to REPO-NAME
===========================

Switch to different repository by name.

QuickSky maintains a global registry of repositories.

Example:
     sky change-to my-other-project

4.6 sky rebase [OPTIONS] [RANGE]
================================

Rebase commits with various options:

'--all'
     Rebase all local changes

'YYYY-MM-DD -> YYYY-MM-DD'
     Rebase commits within date range

'fuck-base'
     Undo last rebase operation

Examples:
     sky rebase --all
     sky rebase 2024-10-01 -> 2024-10-05
     sky rebase fuck-base

4.7 sky reload COMMIT-SHA NEW-MESSAGE
=====================================

Edit past commit message by SHA without breaking history.

Example:
     sky reload a1b2c3d "Correct function name (fixes #42)"


